# ==============================================================================
# EVALUATION: THE BASIC SHAPES & CAMERA POSITIONS
# ==============================================================================

A 0.2 255,255,255 
L 5,10,5 0.6 255,255,255

# --- TEST 1: Camera's position and direction ---
# Instructions: Uncomment the camera you need to test. Keep the others commented.

# 1. "place the camera extending along the x axis pointed towards the coordinates {0, 0, 0}"
# Camera on the X-axis (10, 0, 0) pointing at origin (-1, 0, 0).
C 10,0,0     -1,0,0     70

# 2. "place the camera extending along the y axis pointed towards the coordinates {0, 0, 0}"
# Camera on the Y-axis (0, 10, 0) pointing at origin (0, -1, 0).
# C 0,10,0     0,-1,0     70

# 3. "place the camera extending along the z axis pointed towards the coordinates {0, 0, 0}"
# Camera on the Z-axis (0, 0, 10) pointing at origin (0, 0, -1).
# C 0,0,10     0,0,-1     70

# 4. "place the camera at a random location which isn't on any axis or a diagonal, pointed towards the coordinates {0, 0, 0}"
# Camera placed at (7, 4, 5). The orientation vector is mathematically normalized 
# to point exactly at 0,0,0.
# C 7,4,5      -0.737,-0.421,-0.527  70

# --- TEST 2: The Basic Shapes (Sphere) ---
# "Place a sphere at the coordinates {0, 0, 0}."
# The sphere is perfectly centered at the origin so the camera always looks at it.
sp 0,0,0 2 255,0,0

# --- TEST 3: The Basic Shapes (Plane) ---
# "Place a plane with a 'z' value of null."
# Positioned exactly at Z=0. Dropped to Y=-5 so it acts as a visible floor regardless 
# of whether the evaluator moves the camera to the X, Y, or Z axis.
pl 0,-5,0 0,1,0 0,0,255

# --- TEST 4: The Basic Shapes (Cylinder) ---
# "Place a cylinder extending along the y axis."
# Normal is perfectly vertical (0,1,0). Placed slightly behind the sphere (Z=3) 
# so both are clearly visible from the starting X-axis camera.
cy 0,0,3 0,1,0 2 4 0,255,0
